AI, Unplugged — licensing
=========================

This repository is deliberately licensed in two halves, because it holds two
different kinds of work, and a third that is not ours to license at all.

  Code            — the MIT License below.
                    build.py, tools/, src/js/, src/css/, src/index.html.

  Deck content    — Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International.
                    src/slides/, src/posters/, speaker-notes.md, README.md,
                    CLAUDE.md, docs/, and the prose and figures of the deck.
                    See LICENSE-CONTENT.

  Third-party     — NOT COVERED by either licence. Logos, brand marks and
  assets            screenshots under src/assets/ remain the property of their
                    respective owners, on their own terms. Several are
                    trademarks, which no licence in this repository can grant
                    you any right to use. Note that these assets are inlined
                    into the built files, so the exclusion covers index.html,
                    dist/index.html and posters/*.html as well as the sources
                    they are built from. See ATTRIBUTIONS.md.

Where a single file mixes the two — a slide is markup as well as prose — take
whichever licence is more permissive for what you are actually reusing.

The text above is a description of scope, not part of the licence text that
follows.

